  "bug_description": "### 🕵️‍♂️ Detected with [FACTO](https://github.com/meta-pytorch/FACTO)\n\n### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\nThe CPU clamp operation fully supports broadcasting between the input and the min/max tensors. However MPS fails when the number of dimensions of min or max is greater than that of input tensor\n\n```python\nimport torch\n\ndef test_clamp(device):\n    x = torch.randn(2, 3, device=device)\n    min_t = torch.randn(1, 2, 3, dtype=x.dtype, device=device)\n    max_t = torch.randn(1, 2, 3, dtype=x.dtype, device=device)\n    try:\n        torch.clamp(x, min=min_t, max=max_t)\n        print(f\"clamp test succeeds for device: {device}\")\n    except RuntimeError as e:\n        print(f\"clamp test fails for device: {device}: {e}\")\n\ntest_clamp(device = \"cpu\")\ntest_clamp(device = \"mps\")\n```\n\nterminal output:\n```\nclamp test succeeds for device: cpu\nclamp test fails for device: mps: impl: clamp tensor number of dims must not be greater than that of input tensor\n```\n\n### Versions\n\nnightly\n\ncc @malfet @kulinseth @albanD @DenisVieriu97 @jhavukainen",
